Z||000000||doughboySE||01-22-2000||02:53 PM||||spyder ok now my question is does the size of the box matter for the base it will produce?<BR>would the box be big enough for a 12? as far as the sound goes?<BR>and will this need to be ported and ported to the sides? or up? or where?||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||01-22-2000||05:05 PM||||You have to match up the size of the box with the subwoofer you are using. Most efficient subs that like small boxes are going to need sealed boxes. Here is an example: I have a Rockford-Fosgate 8" Punch sub that needs a box with 0.3 to 0.5 cubic feet of volume. Multiply width X height X depth to get the volume, convert inches to feet first (6 inches equals 0.5 feet). My box is about a 1/3 of a cubic foot which is small. If you wanted to use a ported box, this same subwoofer needs a box between 0.5 to 0.625 cu. ft. in volume. That same model sub in a 10 inch size needs a sealed box that's 0.625 to 0.75 cu. ft. in size. Nearly twice as big as the 8 incher. There are ways to fudge a little, if you stuff the box with poly-fill stuffing, the sub performs as if the box was bigger (this last sentence was a quote from Crutchfield's stereo catalog). Also, when you're building a box, you have to use the right materials, pick up a little guidebook on how to build subwoofer boxes.||||reg||1
Z||000002||doughboySE||01-22-2000||05:16 PM||||WOW NOW IM REALLY CONFUSED <BR>I JUST BOUGHT A SAPHIRE SUB THAT WAS INA PORTED BOX THAT I ACTUALLY HAD IN MY HATCH BACK VW GTI AT ONE TIME<BR>ITS STILL IN THE BOX BUT I AM TAKING IT OUT AND INSTALLING IT IN MY FIERO WHAT YOU THINK? WHERE? AND HOW? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> THANX IN ADVANCE||||reg||1
Z||000003||Spyder||01-22-2000||06:21 PM||||I have the logical answer:<BR>Since I am not familiar with the Saphire sub,<BR>Measure the box you have now, and figure the inside cubic feet then build the new box to have the same cubic feet.  Build the box similar to the drawing in the other post, and put the port firing up toward the ceiling. If you can’t quite build it to that specs add the poly-fill it could help a little.||||reg||1
Z||000004||doughboySE||01-22-2000||08:34 PM||||spyder sorry 1 more question will the sub be totally sealed to port it? it is in the box its in now.<BR>if it  does have to be sealed how the hell do i do that with the box being so narrow ?<BR>just tell me when you are sick of answering questions||||reg||1
Z||000005||Spyder||01-22-2000||10:01 PM||||The box needs to be sealed for the port to work properly, a tuned port.  Use that port from that box. If it won’t fit on top, put it on the side then any where you can make it fit.<BR>Answering  questions gives me something to do at work, I mainly have to just be at work, I feel like a babysitter.||||reg||1
Z||000006||doughboySE||01-22-2000||10:05 PM||||spyder hehehe ok then i dont feel bad<BR>so the bok is sealed does that mean that the face of the sub cant be sticking out like the pic you sent me?<BR>should the only open thing be the port? or is the sub ok to be pointing oput||||reg||1
Z||000007||Spyder||01-22-2000||10:29 PM||||You must cut a hole for the speaker. The box will have two holes, one for the speaker one for the port.  The rest is sealed.  So basically the box you’re building should be just like you’re old one just a different shape.||||reg||10
